<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Editorial standards</span><h1>ToolboxKart editorial policy</h1><p>Our goal is to publish useful, source-backed guidance that separates documented facts, editorial judgment and unverified claims.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container policy-copy"><div class="tool-content"><h2>Research before publication</h2><p>For software, pricing and current technology topics, we review current official product pages, documentation, help centers, changelogs and other primary sources. Independent sources may be used for context, but search snippets and copied comparison lists are not treated as proof.</p><h2>Clear evidence labels</h2><p>We distinguish vendor claims, independent evidence, hands-on observations and editorial inference. We do not say a product was tested unless the test scope and limitations are documented. Hypothetical workflows are labeled as examples, not customer results.</p><h2>Accuracy and updates</h2><p>Prices, plan limits, integrations and platform support are checked on the date stated in each article. Material updates receive a real modified date. We do not change dates merely to make an old page look fresh.</p><h2>Originality and independence</h2><p>ToolboxKart does not copy competitor wording, rankings or review conclusions. Commercial relationships do not determine editorial order or recommendations. Sponsored placements must be labeled and kept separate from the independent comparison.</p><h2>Who is responsible</h2><p>Articles are attributed to their real author. Most current software and SEO coverage is written by <a href="/about-deepak-parmar/">Deepak Parmar</a>. Readers can report an error through the process described in our <a href="/corrections-policy">corrections policy</a>.</p></div></div></section><?php require __DIR__.'/includes/footer.php';?>
